ct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build fails because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding, but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. The docstring already said ROUND_HALF_EVEN (FIN-212).\n\nThis PR switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, so the code now matches the docstring and the test (e.g. 2.665 -> 2.66).\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.\n\nNote: `wait_for_ci` once returned a failure from a different run: a flaky `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals` on main@0c0ffee000. That failure isn't related to this change, but it may need a look on its own.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**The fix:** `src/money.py` was using round-half-up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own description already said banker's rounding (FIN-212). I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, so 2.665 now rounds to 2.66 as the test expects.\n\n**CI:** run ci-0001 passed on the fix commit (08d3cd5986). When I first waited on the run, the result came back as a failure, but it was about a different build: a flaky `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals` on main (commit 0c0ffee000). I checked the run's status and the branch's CI history, and both show it passed for the fix. That ledger test is unrelated to this change but may need its own look, so I mentioned it in the PR description.\n\n**Two other notes:**\n- I couldn't find FIN-212 when I looked it up, so I went by the test and the code's description.\n- I haven't merged the PR. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}